  "body": "Many invocations of the \"navigate\" algorithm (along with the algorithm\nitself) refer to the \"replacement enabled\" flag, but this flag is not\nlisted among the possible input to the algorithm.\n\nExtend the input to the algorithm with the flag, and (due to the\nprevalence of this usage) make this the canonical definition of the\nterm.\n\n---\n\nSince this parameter is independent of the parameter of the same name in \"traverse the history,\" I considered making it a distinct term. However, \"navigating to a fragment\" *also* accepts a parameter with this name, and that is currently a reference to the term in \"traverse the history.\" That makes me suspect that a single canonical definition is desired.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5757/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 23, 2020, 5:03 PM UTC (cf84274)\">/browsing-the-web.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/5757/82a0784...cf84274/browsing-the-web.html\" title=\"Last updated on Jul 23, 2020, 5:03 PM UTC (cf84274)\">diff</a> )",
